{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nPydantic AI 1.107 warns that `openai:` will change from Chat Completions to Responses in v2. Rebar currently relies on Chat Completions for hosted OpenAI and OpenAI-compatible endpoints, so leaving the ambiguous prefix would silently change the wire contract on upgrade. The operator approved preserving Chat Completions with `openai-chat:`; story `upbeat-illadvised-springtail` owns the eventual deliberate Responses migration.\n\n## Approach\nNormalize every rebar-composed or legacy `openai:` Pydantic AI model target to the explicit `openai-chat:` qualifier at the shared primary and model-class/fallback resolution seams. Register the custom-endpoint provider builder for the explicit qualifier so local OpenAI-compatible endpoints keep their existing provider/profile override. Preserve other provider qualifiers unchanged and document `openai-chat:` as the supported Chat Completions spelling.\n\n## Scope\n- Update `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` and `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` so inferred, explicitly qualified, primary, and fallback OpenAI targets resolve to `openai-chat:`.\n- Update `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` so custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints remain routed through rebar’s builder under the explicit qualifier.\n- Strengthen provider-resolution, custom-endpoint, fallback, and library-contract tests in `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py`, `tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py`, `tests/unit/test_llm_provider_factory.py`, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`.\n- Update `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md`, and `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md` to recommend `openai-chat:` while leaving the future Responses migration to `upbeat-illadvised-springtail`.\n\n## Testing\n- Run a warning-as-error oracle through real `infer_model` for inferred, explicit, custom-endpoint, and fallback paths; it must fail before the repair and pass without `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` afterward.\n- Run real loopback custom-endpoint tests and provider/fallback parity tests to prove requests still use Chat Completions and retain structured-output/profile behavior.\n- Run focused provider suites, then repository lint and typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Inferred and legacy-explicit OpenAI model targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by provider-resolution unit and interface tests.\n- [ ] Primary, fallback, hosted, and custom-endpoint model construction emits no `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` with that warning promoted to an error.\n- [ ] The loopback provider contract still sends Chat Completions payloads and preserves the existing custom-endpoint profile override; verified by real-seam provider tests.\n- [ ] Non-OpenAI provider targets and provider-selection conflict checks remain unchanged; verified by provider-parity tests.\n- [ ] User-facing LLM configuration examples name `openai-chat:` for Chat Completions, and the separate Responses-migration story remains the recorded future path.\n- [ ] Focused tests, `make lint`, and `make typecheck` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787026483696823001,"uuid":"d456f646-b4a0-4fb4-b333-aa5cd44e63af"}